{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345448",
      "title": "Alternative: Creating A Shared Handler Function",
      "sourceHash": "1d656bdb623ec61952d5d012db74d51c031facea00e814fcc1a0e48f07961d11",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "Now before we'll dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "into state, React events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "and what we can do with all these things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "I wanna take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "at these change handler functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "because at the moment in this demo application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "I have three change handler functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "One for the title, one for the amount, and one for the date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "Which makes sense since I have these three state slices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.813,
          "en": "and these three main inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "And of course, using this approach is also absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "There's nothing wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "with having these different change handler functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "but I wanna show you an alternative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 49.293,
          "en": "which you also could consider using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "Instead of having all these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 54.09,
          "en": "separate change handler functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.09,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "you could try to create one shared change handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.02,
          "en": "For that, we could create a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 64.053,
          "en": "which could be named inputChangeHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 67.89,
          "en": "And here I'll also create an arrow function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.89,
          "end": 72.12,
          "en": "but I'll now not accept the event argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "But instead here we could accept some identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.38,
          "en": "though this name is up to you because it's your function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.38,
          "end": 81.45,
          "en": "hence your parameter name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 83.10300000000001,
          "en": "And then maybe a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 87.69,
          "en": "And my idea is that I can use this one single function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.69,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "for all my inputs, for all those onChange events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 96.12,
          "en": "And then we can simply identify the different inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.12,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "with help of this identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 101.28,
          "en": "and update the correct state slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "based on the identifier that was passed to this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 106.263,
          "en": "with that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "So in here we could, for example, check if identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 114.42,
          "en": "is equal to, let's say, title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "And if that's the case, we update the title state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 120.58,
          "en": "by calling setEnteredTitle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.563,
          "en": "and setting this equal to the new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.72,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "Else if it's not title, we could check if the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 135.86,
          "en": "is maybe equal to the date here, so if it's equal to date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 143.27,
          "en": "and then update the EnteredDate with the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "And else it must be the amount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore we could then call setEnteredAmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 151.713,
          "en": "and set as equal to value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "So with that, I am calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "all these state updating functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "but I'm now doing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 162.03300000000002,
          "en": "all in one shared change handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.39,
          "end": 166.38,
          "en": "Now we can't use this change handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.38,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "as a input for onChange now though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 171.99,
          "en": "That won't work because as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "React will, in the end, call this function for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "and will pass such an event object to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "and it will definitely not pass an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 182.13,
          "en": "and value to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "We're not going to get those data points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 186.933,
          "en": "when React calls this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 191.013,
          "en": "But we need them for this function to work correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.06,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "Now what we can do here to work around this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "is we can go to this onChange function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.45,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "and instead of passing a pointer to inputChangeHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "as a value to onChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 206.57999999999998,
          "en": "we can pass an arrow function to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.57999999999998,
          "end": 209.04,
          "en": "A new anonymous arrow function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.04,
          "end": 212.1,
          "en": "which we create down there where we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.1,
          "end": 215.04,
          "en": "With that, it's this arrow function that will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.04,
          "end": 217.71,
          "en": "by React whenever this input changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "Therefore this arrow function will receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 221.583,
          "en": "this event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.78,
          "end": 225.6,
          "en": "And in the body of this arrow function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.6,
          "end": 229.74,
          "en": "we can now manually execute inputChangeHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 233.94,
          "en": "So execute this function here, which I just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "We manually execute it by adding parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "And now this code in here will not be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.07,
          "en": "when this line of code here is parsed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.07,
          "end": 244.98,
          "en": "but instead this here will only be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.98,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "when this arrow function here is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 250.35,
          "en": "And that will only be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.35,
          "end": 252.093,
          "en": "when this change event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "But now that we have this wrapper arrow function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 259.74,
          "en": "we have full control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.74,
          "end": 262.89300000000003,
          "en": "over how inputChangeHandler will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.73,
          "end": 266.73,
          "en": "And we can therefore now pass our identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.73,
          "end": 268.77,
          "en": "as a first argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.77,
          "end": 270.9,
          "en": "So for example, title here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.9,
          "end": 274.35,
          "en": "so that for this title input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 276.48,
          "en": "we pass title as an identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.48,
          "end": 279.183,
          "en": "so that we make it into this if branch here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.8,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "And as a second argument, we pass the value that changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "So in this case here, event.target.value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 292.02,
          "en": "just as before, but now in this arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.02,
          "end": 294.42,
          "en": "And with that, we as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.42,
          "end": 297.15,
          "en": "control how this function here will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.15,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "by wrapping it in such a arrow function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "which is the actual function that's passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 304.413,
          "en": "as a value to the onChange prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 308.1,
          "en": "But then we control how this inner function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.1,
          "end": 311.07,
          "en": "will be executed when the change event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.07,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "and we can then use this generic handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 317.7,
          "en": "because now we could use this same code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.7,
          "end": 319.62,
          "en": "or almost the same code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.62,
          "end": 322.98,
          "en": "on the amount input value, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.98,
          "end": 325.623,
          "en": "and pass amount as an identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.52,
          "end": 328.59,
          "en": "But other than that, it's the same code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.59,
          "end": 332.34000000000003,
          "en": "and the function that's being executed is always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.34000000000003,
          "end": 335.94,
          "en": "And this approach simply is an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.94,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "to having multiple specialized handler functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 342.78,
          "en": "As mentioned, there's nothing wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 342.78,
          "end": 345.72,
          "en": "with having these specialized handler functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.72,
          "end": 347.55,
          "en": "but as an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.55,
          "end": 350.523,
          "en": "you could consider using such shared functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 351.72,
          "end": 354.36,
          "en": "With that, I'll get rid of that though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.36,
          "end": 357.9,
          "en": "and move back to the code we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.9,
          "end": 359.97,
          "en": "with the titleChangeHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.97,
          "end": 362.193,
          "en": "and the amountChangeHandler here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 364.23,
          "end": 367.08,
          "en": "But I definitely wanted to share this alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.08,
          "end": 370.32,
          "en": "since it is something you might see in some React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.32,
          "end": 373.23,
          "en": "And since it is something you might want to use yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 373.23,
          "end": 375.093,
          "en": "in your React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}